-<h2 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-size:1.7rem;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:1rem;letter-spacing:-.01em">A flood zone is not the same as a flood history</h2>
-<p style="color:var(--muted);line-height:1.75;max-width:760px;margin-bottom:1rem">A house can be <strong style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600">outside every flood zone and still have flooded</strong>. That trips people up. Flood zones are a prediction of risk; a flood history is a record of what has happened to the specific property. A home can flood from a burst pipe, a storm surge in a freak year, poor drainage, or a neighbor&rsquo;s runoff, none of which shows up on a flood-zone map. Checking the zone alone is not enough. You have to dig into the property&rsquo;s own past.</p>
